# Execution Protocol

- Read `memory-bank/project-brief.md`, `memory-bank/current-state.md`, and `memory-bank/active-context.md` before meaningful work.
- Read the nearest nested `AGENTS.md` when working inside a subsystem that defines one.
- Treat the repo root as canonical. Do not edit `.runtime-wp/` unless the user explicitly asks.
- Prefer canonical category docs in `docs/*` over root `COMPAT_POINTERS.md` (legacy names) or transitional folders.
- Use Plan Mode for multi-file, architectural, or unclear work before implementation.
- Use Browser for visible UI verification and Debug Mode when runtime evidence matters more than code reading.
- Verify changed behavior before claiming success. Use the lightest relevant verification that matches the changed area.
- State what you actually ran. Do not imply runtime or test success without evidence.
- After meaningful work, update `memory-bank/active-context.md` and `memory-bank/progress.md`.
- Use parallel agents and worktrees only for hard refactors, alternatives, or Best-of-N comparisons where isolation is useful.
- If work changes DTOs, REST contracts, auth/trace semantics, generator integration, or mail-ingress workflow, perform an explicit impact check and decide whether `docs/ecosystem/TOPINSTAL_ECOSYSTEM_STATE.md` must be updated.
